WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.850
Now, how.

2
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.875
Personnel actions drive the three
identity events, by code, not by ticket.

3
00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:09.837
A joiner gets an account and
baseline access, ready on day one.

4
00:00:09.837 --> 00:00:12.539
A mover loses the old assignment's access,

5
00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:16.113
gets the new baseline, and
has any exceptions reviewed.

6
00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:21.123
And a leaver is blocked first, the account
disabled and sessions revoked at the

7
00:00:21.123 --> 00:00:24.051
effective separation
time; then credentials,

8
00:00:24.051 --> 00:00:26.826
devices and access are
removed in parallel.

9
00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.838
The book is precise about what
the platform really does.

10
00:00:29.838 --> 00:00:32.341
Revoking sessions stops new tokens,

11
00:00:32.341 --> 00:00:35.762
but tokens already issued
last until they expire.

12
00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:38.565
Privileged leavers need
their own block path,

13
00:00:38.565 --> 00:00:42.988
because the built-in disable task
doesn't support users with admin roles.

14
00:00:42.988 --> 00:00:46.605
And synced users have to be
deleted in Active Directory too,

15
00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:48.599
or the next sync brings them back.

16
00:00:48.599 --> 00:00:53.690
Credentials follow the same events, from
PIV issuance through to termination.
